---
description: Use before merge, release, handoff, or when asked for readiness.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Release Check

- Inspect branch, git status, changed files, verification evidence, migrations/env risk, and rollback path.
- Run the smallest set of existing checks that can falsify the changed surface, then broader release checks when risk justifies them.
- Do not claim ready when required checks failed or were skipped. Report blockers separately from acceptable residual risk.
- For docs/templates/scripts changes, verify generated or bundled resources stay aligned with release checks.
